---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy | aiPressHQ"
  description="aiPressHQ doesn't use cookies. Here's what it uses instead, and why."
>
  <section class="legal-page" aria-labelledby="legal-title">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="label">aiPressHQ / Cookie Policy</span>
      <h1 id="legal-title">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated August 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose legal-body">
      <h2>aiPressHQ does not use cookies</h2>
      <p>
        There's no cookie banner on this site because there's nothing for it to disclose: we don't
        set cookies for analytics, advertising, or tracking, and we don't use any third-party
        service that sets cookies on our behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>What we use instead</h2>
      <p>
        A handful of optional features use your browser's <code>localStorage</code> — a different, device-local
        storage mechanism that, unlike a cookie, is never sent to any server. It exists only to remember
        your own choices between visits:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Saved stories</strong> — articles you've bookmarked to read later.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Recent searches</strong> — your last few searches, shown as quick shortcuts.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> — whether you last chose light or dark mode.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each of these only activates when you use the corresponding feature yourself (clicking save,
        searching, or switching themes) — nothing is stored until you take that action. Because this
        storage is functional and device-local rather than used for tracking or profiling, it
        doesn't require the consent banner that non-essential tracking cookies do.
      </p>

      <h2>Clearing this data</h2>
      <p>
        You can remove saved stories or recent searches individually from within those features, or
        clear everything at once by clearing your browser's site data for aiPressHQ from your
        browser's settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party sites</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles link out to the sources they report on. If you follow one of those links, the
        destination site may set its own cookies according to its own policy — that's outside our
        control once you leave aiPressHQ.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If that ever changes — for example, if a future feature genuinely needs a cookie — this page
        will be updated first, and the date above will change accordingly.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@aipresshq.com"
          >hello@aipresshq.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
